<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Ubuntu on Ricky</title><link>https://linzeyan.github.io/categories/ubuntu/</link><description>Recent content in Ubuntu on Ricky</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2020 13:00:05 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://linzeyan.github.io/categories/ubuntu/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Set interface IP with netplan on Ubuntu 18.04</title><link>https://linzeyan.github.io/posts/2020/20200918-ubuntu-18-04/</link><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2020 13:00:05 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://linzeyan.github.io/posts/2020/20200918-ubuntu-18-04/</guid><description>&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://blog.toright.com/posts/6293/ubuntu-18-04-%E9%80%8F%E9%81%8E-netplan-%E8%A8%AD%E5%AE%9A%E7%B6%B2%E8%B7%AF%E5%8D%A1-ip.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Set interface IP with netplan on Ubuntu 18.04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Following the notes above, check &lt;code&gt;/etc/netplan&lt;/code&gt; and open &lt;code&gt;/etc/netplan/50-cloud-init.yaml&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#abb2bf;background-color:#282c34;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#7f848e"&gt;# This file is generated from information provided by&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#7f848e"&gt;# the datasource. Changes to it will not persist across an instance.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#7f848e"&gt;# To disable cloud-init&amp;#39;s network configuration capabilities, write a file&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#7f848e"&gt;# /etc/cloud/cloud.cfg.d/99-disable-network-config.cfg with the following:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#7f848e"&gt;# network: {config: disabled}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e06c75"&gt;network&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e06c75"&gt;ethernets&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e06c75"&gt;ens192&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e06c75"&gt;dhcp4&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e5c07b"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e06c75"&gt;ens224&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e06c75"&gt;dhcp4&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e5c07b"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e06c75"&gt;version&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#d19a66"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It looks like you can disable cloud network, but I do not use cloud-init, so remove it:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>